    <h1>The Natural Law Resurgence Movement</h1>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap narrow-wrap prose-page movement">
    <p>The annual event devoted to &ldquo;Natural Law and the Renewal of Western Civilization,&rdquo; in Washington D.C., forms part of a greater effort coined the &ldquo;Natural Law Resurgence Movement&rdquo;: a worldwide coordinated endeavor dedicated to the natural law (research, study, discussion, publication, formation, teaching).</p>
    <p>Scholars, many of whom maintain close working relationships with politicians and state leaders, have been gathering together to advance serious reflection on the general principles of morality that give fundamental purpose to: 1) man as a social being with a natural aptitude for political society and a compelling need for it; 2) the family based on marriage between one man and woman, the first natural society: school of love and virtue ethics; and 3) the State, also a natural society that offers the means to the common good of men, at the national level, which has a plenitude of sovereignty for international relationship with other nation states.</p>
    <p>The movement seeks not primarily to settle theoretical disagreements among competing schools of natural law, but to recover a shared foundation for moral reasoning and public discourse, particularly in response to contemporary challenges in social, political and legal life to the existence of objective truth and the capacity of human reason to know it and to accurately assess and limit unjust laws.</p>

    <h2>Key Organizations Promoting &ldquo;Natural Law and the Renewal of Western Civilization&rdquo;</h2>
    <p>Contributions to the movement are happening at many different conference venues, publishing houses, and academic institutions around the world. Much information about the same are noted on the website of <a href="https://www.iurisnaturalis.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i>Iuris Naturalis Societas</i></a>.</p>
    <p>Notable organizations that are part of the Natural Law Resurgence Movement primarily because of their past collaboration and cooperation that have led the event, &ldquo;Natural Law and the Renewal of Western Civilization,&rdquo; include</p>
    <ul>
      <li><i>Lumen de Lumine</i> Foundation (LdL): promotes the activities of canonist and natural law expert, Cardinal Raymond Leo Burke;</li>
      <li><a href="https://icjurist.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">International Catholic Jurists Forum</a> (ICJF): co-organizes natural law activities, conferences and publications with other entities;</li>
      <li><a href="https://fundacionveritas.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i>Fundación Véritas</i></a> (FV): is sponsoring the creation of a center devoted to natural law and related programs at the <i>Universidad del Medio Atlántico</i> (UNAM), in the Canary Islands, Spain;</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.iurisnaturalis.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i>Iuris Naturalis Societas</i></a> (INS): organizes activities and shares information and materials about the natural law with its large group of members spread throughout the world, many of whom are professors of legal philosophy; and</li>
      <li><a href="https://subsidium.online/author.php?slug=iain-benson" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i>Subsidium</i></a>: considers many issues especially ones of international significance through the lens of the principle of subsidiarity.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Important Previous Initiatives</h2>
    <p>Notable examples of activities involving members of the above group that might be categorized as falling under the umbrella of the &ldquo;Natural Law Resurgence Movement,&rdquo; include the following:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>October 1&ndash;3, 2026, <a href="https://liquid1188.github.io/icjf-website/files/Natural-Law-Conference-Rome-October-2026-Program.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">A Natural Law Discussion: From the Ancients to Contemporary Thought. The Crisis and Renewal of Natural Law in the Modern World</a>, Rome, Italy. Opening lecture by Cardinal Raymond Leo Burke. It was co-sponsored by LdL, ICJF, FV, INS and other entities.</li>
      <li>November 6&ndash;7, 2025, <a href="https://www.avemarialaw.edu/artificial-intelligence/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The 5th Biennial Conference on Religion and Politics, Supreme Guarantee against All Abuses of Power? Question of God and Existence of Politics, In Memory of John Paul II</a>, in Warsaw, Poland. The panel discussion on &ldquo;Truth and AI&rdquo; was organized and co-sponsored by Subsidium-ICJF and other entities.</li>
      <li>September 25&ndash;27, 2025, Truth, Freedom of Speech, and Modern-day Censorship, Washington D.C. Co-sponsored as Subsidium-ICJF along with other entities.</li>
      <li>July 13&ndash;18, 2025, <a href="https://www.iurisnaturalis.com/ver-ficha/5242" target="_blank" rel="noopener">First World Congress of the Iuris Naturalis Societas: Natural Law and Human Rights</a>, Madrid, Spain. Co-sponsored as Subsidium-ICJF with the organizer: INS.</li>
      <li>April 30 &ndash; May 5, 2025, Natural Law Summer School: Justice and Solidarity, co-sponsored by Subsidium-ICJF with the Jagiellonian University (and various departments) in Kraków, Poland.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Ongoing Projects</h2>
    <h3>The UDHR Project: The New York Consensus Declaration</h3>
    <p>From July 2025 to July 2026, a group of ICJF advisors (many of them qualified lawyers with practical legal experience) considered the explicit and implicit natural law foundations of the 1948 Universal Declaration of Human Rights (UDHR).</p>
    <p>From the outset, contributing scholars viewed the UDHR as necessarily imperfect due to the frailties of the diplomatic process, and the limited historical perspective at the time, where certain matters could be taken for granted or had not yet been identified as problematic. Certainly, there are many contemporary challenges for political leaders given the rise of &ldquo;gender ideology,&rdquo; which has contributed to the proliferation of &ldquo;new rights,&rdquo; while other anti-life ideologies have promoted abortion and euthanasia. These concerns stand alongside the ever-expanding categories of &ldquo;discrimination&rdquo; (e.g., &ldquo;sexual orientation&rdquo; and &ldquo;gender identity,&rdquo; hate speech and so forth) that are being used as a hammer to persecute Christians in the courts (see the book <a href="https://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/equality-and-non-discrimination-jane-f-adolphe/1131291618" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i>Equality and Non-Discrimination: Catholic Roots, Current Challenges</i></a>).</p>
    <p>With these issues in mind, the said group created an outcome document entitled &ldquo;The New York Consensus Declaration&rdquo; (NYCD) to reflect a possible use of it by state leaders during United Nations General Assembly (UNGA) meetings, in New York. An explanation note, largely drafted by the head of <a href="https://subsidium.online/author.php?slug=iain-benson" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i>Subsidium</i></a>, explains the implicit and explicit natural law foundation in more detail with reference to common challenges and misconceptions.</p>

    <h2>Increased Cooperation with Central and South America</h2>
    <p>From October 26&ndash;28, 2026, <a href="https://jornadasderechonatural.com/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The XVIII International Natural Law Conference</a> was held in Santiago, Chile. For the first time, Australian and European scholars (advisors to ICJF and members of their own organizations INS, FV, and Subsidium) participated in the gathering held in Santiago, Chile.</p>
    <p>The hope is that some of the upcoming conferences can be held in Europe, the United States or Australia in an effort to further solidify the global effort to consider the foundational principles of natural law and their contemporary applications.</p>
